-- title:
--   Initial form of the moduli j-invariant on Drinfeld charts
-- statement:
--   Fix primes $q\ge 5$ and $\ell\ge 3$ with $\ell\neq q$, and $M'\neq 0$ divisible by neither; let $L$ be a characteristic-zero field that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of conductor $q\ell$, with $\zeta$ a primitive $q$-th and $\xi$ a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity. Let $K\subseteq L((t))$ be the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image of the function field of level $(q\ell)^2M'$ attached to the kernel $H$ of $(\mathbb{Z}/(q\ell)^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^\times$; let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$, uniformiser $\varpi$, with $q\in\mathfrak m_A$ and $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, acting on $K$ compatibly, and let $j\in K$, $j\neq 0$, be the Laurent series $q$-expansion of the modular $j$-function. On the two-chart integral model, the pushout of $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the integral closures of $A[j]$ and $A[j^{-1}]$ in $K$, let $z$ be a point at which the pullback of $\varpi$ has germ in the maximal ideal of the stalk, and $y$ a point of the $j$-finite chart $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the chart algebra mapping to $z$, assumed supersingular in the sense that every homomorphism from the chart algebra to an algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ with kernel $y$ sends $j$ to an element of $\operatorname{ssJSet} q\,\Omega$, i.e. to a $j$-invariant all of whose elliptic models have trivial $q$-torsion. Let further $W$ be a complete discrete valuation ring, $\sigma:A\to W$ a ring homomorphism carrying $\varpi$ to a uniformiser, $f,u,v\in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u,v$ units and $f\equiv X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1 \pmod{(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}}$, and $e$ a ring isomorphism from the $\mathfrak m$-adic completion of the stalk at $z$ onto $S:=W[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma\varpi)v-fu)$. Assume $e$ carries the germ of the pullback of each $a\in A$ to the class of $C(\sigma a)$. Then the Laurent series $\operatorname{jqNModC} L\,(q\ell)$ lies in $K$ and in the $j$-finite chart algebra, and there are $a_0\in W$, $e_0\ge 1$ and $h\in(X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ such that, first, for all $a,b\in W$ not both in $\mathfrak m_W$ with $a^qb-ab^q\in\mathfrak m_W$, the value $\sum_{i=0}^{e_0}h_{(i,e_0-i)}a^ib^{e_0-i}$ of the degree-$e_0$ part of $h$ is a unit of $W$, and second, in $S$ the image under $e$ of the germ at $z$ of that element of the chart algebra differs from the class of $C(a_0)$ by the class of $h$.
--
--   This is the statement, in the formal Drinfeld-chart frame, of the Katz–Mazur analysis of the moduli $j$-invariant near a supersingular point: after subtracting the $j$-value of the canonical unramified lift, its germ is $(X_0,X_1)$-adically pure of some order $e_0$, with initial form invertible along all directions killed by $X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1$. It is used in the construction of the completed local charts of the integral model of the modular curve of level $H$ at supersingular points, feeding the Drinfeld-chart presentation theorem that cites it.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_AuxLevel_exists_sub_const_eq_mk_of_mem_pow_isUnit_homogeneous_drinfeldChart_of_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_stalk.lean

